{
    "siteID": "otrdoo430x42",
    "siteDescription": "",
    "siteName": "Animal housing - Italy",
    "siteMethodClassification": "",
    "siteType": "animal housing",
    "siteLocation": "Italy",
    "cycleID": "7efx0enper3k",
    "cycleDescription": "Permanent Meadows Farm - representative of farms located in the Po plain where the cattle were fed principally with forage, compound feed and small quantities of alfalfa and corn feed, without silage feed and protein ingredients. In this system, the forage has spontaneously grown solely in the grassland of the farm and, during warmer seasons, has been left to dry into hay. Therefore, the milk produced is commonly known as \u201chay milk\u201d, destined to produce Grana Padano cheese as well. Differentiating from the other plain systems, in PMF, meadows were never alternated with other crops, and there was no ploughing or harrowing, only mowing and irrigation. The cattle had the possibility to go in the outdoor paddock during the summer season.",
    "cycleMethodClassification": "non-verified survey data",
    "functionalUnit": "relative",
